# 14. Conclusion

The application was vulnerable to **Web Cache Poisoning** due to its unsafe handling of the `X-Forwarded-Host` header combined with an improperly configured caching mechanism.

By poisoning the cache, an attacker could force legitimate users to load attacker-controlled JavaScript, potentially leading to session hijacking, phishing attacks, or complete client-side compromise.

This vulnerability demonstrates how seemingly harmless proxy headers can become critical attack vectors when combined with caching misconfigurations.
